            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "There is solution:\n```diff\ndiff --git a/Cython/Compiler/ExprNodes.py b/Cython/Compiler/ExprNodes.py\nindex e88139c59..492145a88 100644\n--- a/Cython/Compiler/ExprNodes.py\n+++ b/Cython/Compiler/ExprNodes.py\n@@ -6312,6 +6312,9 @@ class CallNode(ExprNode):\n                 self.type = result_type\n             elif result_type.equivalent_type:\n                 self.type = result_type.equivalent_type\n+            else:\n+                self.type = result_type\n+                self.result_ctype = result_type\n\n     def analyse_as_type_constructor(self, env):\n         \"\"\"\ndiff --git a/Cython/Compiler/Optimize.py b/Cython/Compiler/Optimize.py\nindex bf9bbaf04..27bb53c71 100644\n--- a/Cython/Compiler/Optimize.py\n+++ b/Cython/Compiler/Optimize.py\n@@ -3390,7 +3390,7 @@ class OptimizeBuiltinCalls(Visitor.NodeRefCleanupMixin,\n         else:\n             type_name = 'Object'\n         if len(args) == 1:\n-            return ExprNodes.PythonCapiCallNode(\n+            ret_node = ExprNodes.PythonCapiCallNode(\n                 node.pos, \"__Pyx_Py%s_Pop\" % type_name,\n                 self.PyObject_Pop_func_type,\n                 args=[obj],\n@@ -3398,6 +3398,7 @@ class OptimizeBuiltinCalls(Visitor.NodeRefCleanupMixin,\n                 is_temp=node.is_temp,\n                 utility_code=load_c_utility('pop'),\n             )\n+            return ret_node.coerce_to(node.type, self.current_env())\n         elif len(args) == 2:\n             index = unwrap_coerced_node(args[1])\n             py_index = ExprNodes.NoneNode(index.pos)\n~\n```\n\nBut it am not 100% sure about it whether is 100% correct + it requires to introduce `coerce_to()` to every `PythonCapiCallNode()` which I am not sure if there is not better solution...",
