        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I think we have to take care to keep a Python object type as the return type of the call, because that's what it returns. We do not get the final coerced C type back. That is something that needs to be done by a coercion outside of the node, and the `CallNode` can set up the coercion of its return value during type analysis. It's too late to do it during the method optimisation.",
